    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Elections",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4382\n\nSPONSOR: SAVINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to the election of county committee members\n\n \nPURPOSE:  OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to authorize temporary changes to the county\ncommittee reorganization process in order to ensure New Yorkers' safety\nduring political processes that take place during the current COVID-19\npandemic.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 provides that notwithstanding section 2-106 of the Election\nLaw, a majority of the executive committee of a county committee may\nadopt a temporary amendment to its rules, filed with the state and local\nboards of elections prior to March 2, 2021, that members of such county\ncommittee elected in an odd year whose terms are expiring in 2021 may\nremain in such office for an additional one-year term.  Such county\ncommittee members shall be required to run in 2022 for a one-year term.\nIn 2023, and thereafter, such committee members shall run for two-year\nterms.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe state of emergency caused by the coronavirus pandemic necessitates a\nlimitation on petitioning activities. However, certain counties are\nrequired to elect new county committee members in 2021. Since county\ncommittee is the most local level of party governance, representing an\nElection District, there would inevitably be health concerns if all\ncounty committee candidates - in the boroughs of New York City there\ncould be thousands - would be required to go door-to-door in order to\ncollect petition signatures. Therefore, this bill authorizes county\ncommittees to holdover its current membership for one year and instead\nrequire such committee members to run in 2022 for a one-year term\ninstead of a two-year term in order to return to the regular political\ncalendar.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNot yet determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
